1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,193
The calendar works with workflows and with AI assistants.

2
00:00:05,193 --> 00:00:11,249
Workflows can start when an event changes, and can add, move, find and cancel events.

3
00:00:11,249 --> 00:00:16,307
An AI assistant can read your calendar, find free time, and book, move

4
00:00:16,307 --> 00:00:18,437
and cancel events for you.

5
00:00:18,437 --> 00:00:20,300
This video shows both.

6
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,401
Much of calendar work is routine.

7
00:00:27,401 --> 00:00:31,056
Someone books time off, and a cover plan is needed.

8
00:00:31,056 --> 00:00:35,480
A meeting is about to start, and its attendees need the agenda.

9
00:00:36,230 --> 00:00:39,406
Workflows watch for those moments, and act.

10
00:00:39,406 --> 00:00:44,850
The calendar adds events, tasks and a free time search to the workflow editor.

11
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:50,376
AI assistants do the other kind of routine work, the questions people ask.

12
00:00:50,376 --> 00:00:52,107
What is on my calendar?

13
00:00:52,107 --> 00:00:53,480
When can we meet?

14
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,510
Move that meeting to Friday.

15
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:00,170
Both act with the access of a person, and never beyond it.

16
00:01:04,363 --> 00:01:06,841
Open Workflows, and edit a workflow.

17
00:01:06,841 --> 00:01:11,147
The Activities panel lists everything you can drag onto the canvas.

18
00:01:11,147 --> 00:01:14,923
Search for Calendar, and the calendar's activities appear.

19
00:01:15,374 --> 00:01:19,339
The Events tab shows the events that can start a workflow:

20
00:01:19,339 --> 00:01:26,154
an event created, updated, cancelled or deleted, an attendee invited, and an attendee's answer received.

21
00:01:26,154 --> 00:01:30,924
With Calendar Reminders on, there are also Starting Soon and Completed.

22
00:01:31,374 --> 00:01:34,718
The Tasks tab shows what a workflow can do:

23
00:01:34,718 --> 00:01:41,404
create, update, cancel, get and find events, add and remove an attendee, and find free time.

24
00:01:41,855 --> 00:01:45,095
This workflow starts with Calendar Event Created.

25
00:01:45,095 --> 00:01:46,508
Open its settings.

26
00:01:46,508 --> 00:01:51,869
It can be limited to some calendars, some types of calendar, and some kinds of event.

27
00:01:51,869 --> 00:01:55,875
Here it only reacts to Out of office events on team calendars.

28
00:01:56,326 --> 00:01:58,953
The second step is Create Calendar Event.

29
00:01:58,953 --> 00:02:01,972
It adds a meeting to the design team's calendar.

30
00:02:01,972 --> 00:02:06,333
Its text fields take values from the event that started the workflow, so

31
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:08,346
the meeting is named after it.

32
00:02:12,547 --> 00:02:17,607
Add an Out of office event for Riley Ortiz on the design team's calendar.

33
00:02:26,170 --> 00:02:28,921
Open Workflows, then Instances.

34
00:02:28,921 --> 00:02:33,010
The workflow started by itself, and has finished.

35
00:02:33,461 --> 00:02:36,798
On the calendar, the cover plan meeting is there.

36
00:02:36,798 --> 00:02:42,561
The workflow created it, and a change made by a workflow never starts the workflow again.

37
00:02:46,764 --> 00:02:51,257
With the AI features on, an AI profile can use calendar tools.

38
00:02:51,257 --> 00:02:55,552
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profiles, and edit a profile.

39
00:02:55,552 --> 00:02:59,914
On the Capabilities tab, the Calendar group lists six tools.

40
00:03:00,364 --> 00:03:06,743
List calendars, Find calendar events, Find free time, Create calendar event, Move calendar

41
00:03:06,743 --> 00:03:09,334
event, and Cancel calendar event.

42
00:03:09,334 --> 00:03:14,184
Tick the ones this assistant may use, or select them all, and save.

43
00:03:15,784 --> 00:03:19,083
Here is an example of what people can then ask.

44
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:23,999
The assistant uses Find calendar events to answer what is on the calendar

45
00:03:23,999 --> 00:03:27,234
this week, for up to sixty-two days at a time.

46
00:03:27,984 --> 00:03:33,080
Asked to find thirty minutes with Sam on Thursday, it uses Find free time.

47
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:37,411
That looks at the people, and at calendars such as a room, for

48
00:03:37,411 --> 00:03:39,194
up to thirty-one days.

49
00:03:39,944 --> 00:03:43,499
Asked to book it, it uses Create calendar event.

50
00:03:43,499 --> 00:03:49,884
Asked to move or cancel the meeting, it uses Move calendar event and Cancel calendar event.

51
00:03:50,634 --> 00:03:54,494
The tools act for the person who is signed in, with that person's

52
00:03:54,494 --> 00:03:56,124
access to each calendar.

53
00:03:56,124 --> 00:03:58,624
They refuse anyone who is not signed in.

54
00:04:02,824 --> 00:04:07,282
Changes made by a workflow are recorded as made by a workflow, and

55
00:04:07,282 --> 00:04:12,234
workflows ignore them by default, so a workflow cannot start itself again.

56
00:04:12,984 --> 00:04:16,781
Starting Soon and Completed need Calendar Reminders.

57
00:04:16,781 --> 00:04:20,904
They run once for every occurrence, even after a restart.

58
00:04:21,654 --> 00:04:23,861
AI tools need the AI feature.

59
00:04:23,861 --> 00:04:29,094
Appointment booking for customers has its own tools, covered with Scheduling.

60
00:04:31,094 --> 00:04:35,828
Workflows react to the calendar and change it, and AI assistants read it

61
00:04:35,828 --> 00:04:39,167
and book on your behalf, always with your access.

62
00:04:39,167 --> 00:04:40,744
Thanks for watching.

